    "why": "Event-contract and options revenue must carry the quarter while crypto stays weak \u2014 that mix is what the multiple is paying for."
  },
  "reasons": [
    "Because event-contract volume ran about 60% above May in preliminary June 2026 data and prediction markets keep widening into sports and culture, the newest revenue line can beat without crypto.",
    "The June 2026 retail rebound bypassed crypto, but US retail trading runs above $70 billion a day, so equities and options volume \u2014 where Robinhood earns more per trade \u2014 carries the quarter.",
    "Goodwill rose 115% in 2025, so part of the base is bought; but SG&A [selling, general and administrative costs] rose 0.6% QoQ while revenue rose 22.6% QoQ (32.3% YoY), and bought revenue cannot widen that gap."
  ],
  "watch": [
    "Event-contract revenue: confirms if it grows again off Q2's record; breaks if the June surge faded or CFTC listing rules bite.",
    "Crypto transaction revenue: confirms if the decline is contained; breaks if it drags total transaction revenue below the $1.43B consensus.",
    "EPS against $0.64417: confirms at or above; breaks on any miss, because four straight beats have set the bar high.",
    "Adjusted OpEx: confirms at or below $2.775B; breaks above the top of the $2.675B-$2.775B range."
